169	Korea Advanced Institute Of Science Technology Kaist Kaist Scholarship	Asia	Luar Negeri (Korea Selatan)	S2	Beasiswa - Korea Advanced Institute of Science & Technology (KAIST) - KAIST Scholarship untuk jenjang S2 dengan tipe Fully Funded di South Korea	17 Maret 2026	Fully Funded	Matematika, Fisika, Kimia, Ilmu Biologi, Teknik Elektro, Teknik Mesin, Teknik Robotika, Teknik Sipil, Teknik Dirgantara, Teknik Industri, Teknik Umum, Ilmu Material dan Teknik, Teknik Biomedis, Hukum dan Studi Hukum, Studi Budaya dan Agama, Administrasi Bisnis	• Full tuition grant: 4 semesters for Master’s, 10 semesters for M.S-Ph.D. integrated 8 semesters for Ph.D students\n• Monthly stipend guarantee: The KAIST Scholarship provides a monthly stipend, empowering many international students to attain financial independence from their home countries. The stipend amount depends on factors such as department, program, advisor, or involvement in research. For additional details, please contact the relevant department/program staff or  the intended advisor.\n• Premium for National Health Insurance subscription: actual costs * The rate and coverage may vary by your participation in research projects and performance.\n• KGPS is a signature scholarship program for Master’s or M.S.-Ph.D -integrated program students. Awardees will receive full tuition fee waivers and KRW 1,000,000 per each month as stipend for four regular semesters of education. KAIST Scholarship applicants are automatically registered for KGPS review that there is no additional procedure to take to apply for KGPS.	AGE No age requirement GPA Min. GPA: 2 out of 4.00 ENGLISH TEST IELTS: min. 7 TOEFL iBT: min. 83 TOEIC NATIONALITY Indonesian OTHER LANGUAGE Not required STANDARDIZED TEST Not required DOCUMENTS Document Checklist: A Copy of Application Form Statement of Financial Resources (Online Application) Recommendation Letters Certified Degree / Diploma Certified Transcripts Certified English Proficiency Test (EPT) Reports (TOEFL