214	Indonesia Austria Scholarship Programme Iasp	Eropa	Luar Negeri (Austria)	S3	Beasiswa - Indonesia-Austria Scholarship Programme (IASP) untuk jenjang S3 dengan tipe Fully Funded di Austria	1 Maret 2026	Fully Funded	Ilmu Alam Terapan, Studi Pertanian, Technical Sciences, Ilmu Kesehatan, School of Medicine, Humanities, Inequalities and Social Science, Seni Rupa	• Supplementary grant, own funds are required!:\n• Tuition-free education\n• Monthly living allowance: EUR 1150 (increase to EUR 1300 already approved, subject to official authorization)\n• International airfares (tickets): at cost, maximum of EUR 1000\n• Monthly mobility allowance: EUR 80\n• Monthly family allowance: EUR 250 for spouse and EUR 250 for one child max. (increase to EUR 325 already approved, subject to official authorization). Family allowance is provided only in the 2nd and 3rd year of study, if the family is invited by the student.\n• Assistance in arranging accommodation and health insurance\n• Duration:\n• 36 months (9 months preparatory phase at the beginning; possibility to extend up to a maximum of 2 semesters on a case-by-case basis)\n• Quota:\n• up to 15 scholarships per study year	AGE Max Age: 35 GPA No GPA requirement ENGLISH TEST IELTS: min. 7 TOEFL iBT: min. 90 TOEFL ITP NATIONALITY Indonesian OTHER LANGUAGE Not required STANDARDIZED TEST Not required DOCUMENTS Application form: The following documents have to be submitted: 1. Letter of acceptance from a supervisor of the Austrian host university or an unconditional Letter of Admission (LoA) 2. Research Proposal (5-10 pages) The applicant's proposal for an innovative research project should focus on specific research questions, and contain a clear and detailed description of the research directions and objectives as well as the methodological approach. The research proposal has to be agreed on with the future supervisor in Austria and is expected to include: a clear problem description a literature review (incl. references) expected